<newsitem itemid="384273" id="root" date="1997-02-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Mobile raises half yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Mobile raises half yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31.</p>
<p>	     (millions of rands unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		5.2		vs 4.4</p>
<p>    Interim div (cts)    1.0		vs 0.9</p>
<p>    Attrib income	 46.3		vs 38.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 12.4		vs 12.1</p>
<p>    Tax			0.6		vs  0.9</p>
<p>    Interest		17.8		vs 15.1</p>
<p>    Turnover		31.7		vs 28.3</p>
<p>Div payable April 9</p>
<p>On register March 7</p>
<p>Full name -  Mobile Industries Ltd</p>
<p>(industrial-transportation)</p>
<p>NOTE - Shareholders will be offered a capitalisation share award in lieu of the dividend in the ratio of 0.416667 shares for every existing Mobile share held.</p>
<p>Mobile's earnings are derived from the group's 48 percent interest in Trencor Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
